## Why This Is Asked
This problem assesses mastery of graph algorithms on DAGs, including topological sorting, feasibility verification under ordered constraints, and shortest-path computation.

## Key Concepts
- Topological sort for DAGs
- DAG shortest-path DP (O(|V| + |E|))
- Feasibility checking with ordered mandatory edges
- Path reconstruction via predecessor pointers

## Code Example
```javascript
function shortestConstrainedPath(G, S, T, M) {
  const topo = topoSort(G);
  const idx = (v) => topo.indexOf(v);

  const canReach = (from, to) => {
    if (idx(from) >= idx(to)) return false;
    const reachable = new Set([from]);
    for (let i = idx(from); i < idx(to); i++) {
      for (const edge of G.adj[topo[i]]) {
        if (idx(edge.to) < idx(to)) reachable.add(edge.to);
      }
    }
    return reachable.has(to);
  };

  const points = [S, ...M.map(e => e[0]), ...M.map(e => e[1]), T];
  for (let i = 0; i < points.length - 1; i++) {
    if (!canReach(points[i], points[i + 1])) return null;
  }

  const segmentCost = (src, dst) => {
    const dist = {}; dist[src] = 0;
    for (let i = idx(src); i < idx(dst); i++) {
      const u = topo[i];
      for (const edge of G.adj[u]) {
        if (idx(edge.to) < idx(dst)) {
          if (dist[u] + edge.w < (dist[edge.to] ?? Infinity)) {
            dist[edge.to] = dist[u] + edge.w;
          }
        }
      }
    }
    return dist[dst];
  };

  let total = 0;
  const fullPath = [S];
  for (const [u, v, w] of M) {
    total += w;
    const seg = segmentCost(fullPath[fullPath.length - 1], u);
    if (seg === undefined) return null;
    total += seg;
  }
  const finalSeg = segmentCost(M[M.length - 1][1], T);
  if (finalSeg === undefined) return null;
  return total + finalSeg;
}
```

## Why This Question Matters

This problem evaluates a candidate's ability to extend standard grid DP problems with additional state dimensions. Modeling exact-turn constraints is essential in path-planning scenarios such as robot navigation, vehicle routing, and game movement where turn penalties or restrictions exist.

## Core Concepts

- **State Design**: Extending traditional grid DP with turn count and last direction dimensions
- **Transition Logic**: Increment turn count when direction changes between moves
- **Space Optimization**: Using row-wise or 2-layer rolling arrays to reduce memory from O(n*m*K) to O(m*K)
- **Edge Cases**: Handling obstacles, impossible turn requirements, and boundary conditions

## Reference Implementation

```javascript
function maxPathSumWithTurns(grid, K) {
  const n = grid.length, m = grid[0].length;
  const INF = -Infinity;
  const dp = Array.from({ length: n }, () =>
    Array.from({ length: m }, () =>
      Array.from({ length: K + 1 }, () => [INF, INF])
    )
  );

  dp[0][0][0][0] = dp[0][0][0][1] = grid[0][0];

  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    for (let j = 0; j < m; j++) {
      if (grid[i][j] === -1) continue;
      for (let t = 0; t <= K; t++) {
        if (j + 1 < m && grid[i][j+1] !== -1) {
          const newTurn = t + (i > 0 ? 1 : 0);
          if (newTurn <= K) {
            dp[i][j+1][newTurn][0] = Math.max(
              dp[i][j+1][newTurn][0],
              dp[i][j][t][1] + grid[i][j+1]
            );
          }
          dp[i][j+1][t][0] = Math.max(dp[i][j+1][t][0], dp[i][j][t][0] + grid[i][j+1]);
        }
        if (i + 1 < n && grid[i+1][j] !== -1) {
          const newTurn = t + (j > 0 ? 1 : 0);
          if (newTurn <= K) {
            dp[i+1][j][newTurn][1] = Math.max(
              dp[i+1][j][newTurn][1],
              dp[i][j][t][0] + grid[i+1][j]
            );
          }
          dp[i+1][j][t][1] = Math.max(dp[i+1][j][t][1], dp[i][j][t][1] + grid[i+1][j]);
        }
      }
    }
  }

  const result = Math.max(...dp[n-1][m-1].flat());
  return result === INF ? -1 : result;
}
```

